Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to init/main.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    the init thread's stack (kernel heap)   16 KiB -> 4 KiB (it opens three
                                            files and starts the shell; 2,460
                                            bytes used, measured in Renode;
                                            3 KiB with its 1 KiB guard was
                                            too little)

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/init/main.ad --label b/init/main.ad init/main.ad <copy>

--- a/init/main.ad
+++ b/init/main.ad
@@ -62,6 +62,6 @@
     board_display_start()               # the console on a display too, where the board has one
     board_input_start()                 # ... and a keyboard beside the UART, where it has one
     console_rx_enable()
-    thread_create("init", cast[uint64](&init_main), 0, 2, 16384, 0)
+    thread_create("init", cast[uint64](&init_main), 0, 2, 4096, 0)
     sched_start()
     return 0
